      ],
      "budget_share": 0.2,
      "why": "Baseline pipelined family (m=1) provides a reference point and covers the high-Fmax corner. It is a special case of pipelined_m, so it helps confirm that register sharing reduces area. Small budget because pipelined_m with m>1 should dominate for area."
    },
    {
      "family": "pipelined_m",
      "ranges": [
        {"param": "data_width", "low": 11, "high": 16, "choices": null},
        {"param": "n_iter", "low": 10, "high": 18, "choices": null},
        {"param": "angle_guard", "low": -1, "high": 2, "choices": null},
        {"param": "frac_guard", "low": 0, "high": 3, "choices": null},
        {"param": "rounding", "low": null, "high": null, "choices": ["trunc", "round"]},
        {"param": "m", "low": 2, "high": 8, "choices": null}
      ],
      "budget_share": 0.8,
      "why": "Main family for area minimisation. Registering every m stages reduces flip-flop count while keeping 1 result/cycle, so larger m can yield smaller area. The m dimension is the key trade-off between FF count and combinational depth; throughput constraint (>=1 MSPS) is easily met even at low Fmax. Majority budget to explore m and the accuracy boundary."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "The spec requires max_abs_err <= 2^-10, which sets hard lower bounds: data_width >= 11 (since output LSB = 2^-(W-2) and half-LSB must be <= 2^-10) and n_iter >= 10 (CORDIC angle approximation error ~2^-N). Throughput >= 1 MSPS is trivially satisfied by both pipelined families (1 result/cycle) even at low Fmax, so area is the only binding objective. We search both families over the accuracy boundary (W 11..16, N 10..18) and guard bits, with pipelined_m receiving most budget because its m parameter (2..8) allows trading FFs for combinational depth, directly reducing area. The ranges cover designs from just meeting 10-bit accuracy up to ~14-bit accuracy, enabling the Pareto front to be mapped. No infeasibility is expected; if no design meets the error constraint, code will report it."
}

{
  "decision": "stop",
  "rationale": "Final round: the feasible front is established and the spec is satisfiable. Constraints are met with margin — throughput best seen 190 MSPS vs >=1 required (0% violations), and max_abs_err best 2^-13.13 vs <=2^-10 required. The Pareto front spans area_um2 18406..32615 against the HV reference 40000 and accuracy_bits 10.1..13.1 against reference 10, so it covers a wide portion of both objective ranges (HV 4.782e+04). The selection rule (min area_um2) picks pipelined_m [data_width=16 n_iter=12 angle_guard=0 frac_guard=0 rounding=trunc m=8] at area_um2=18406, accuracy_bits=10.14 (max_abs_err=0.000887 <= 0.000976562), throughput 23.6 MSPS >= 1 — a valid, constraint-satisfying optimum. No infeasibility: every constraint is achieved by multiple designs. Stopping."
  ,"next_plan": null
}
